 },
 "memo": "Read each cell in full, then grouped policies by the action they ask for (or, for background cells, the kind of fact stated). Kept a running label list and reused labels for the same idea across cells (e.g. 'Citing and disclosing AI use', 'Verifying AI output', 'Keeping data out of AI tools', 'AI supporting rather than replacing learning', 'Presenting AI work as one's own', 'AI's effect on learning'). Hard calls: in the student university restrict cell I merged personal-data and course-material upload rules into one 'Keeping data out of AI tools' group to stay within 7 groups; in the student course restrict cell 'assume no AI when unsure' policies were folded into the instructor-permission group because both set a no-AI default; submission-format rules (handwritten scans, transcript links, statements for extension points) form a small group of their own; in the large instructor before-course cell, misuse-prevention culture items (non-punitive approach, normalizing struggle) were grouped with penalty planning; single-policy groups were kept only where the policy was clearly distinct (e.g. assistive technology, opting out of AI grading, instructors disclosing their own AI use)."
}